                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is great! I have never written a review, but I think now is the time.\n\nPros:\n\n-Waba is super fun to play with. You really do feel like you are touching it. He feels alive and has emotions.\n-The animations are beautiful and fluid.\n-The inventory/environment/tool system is very intuitive and takes an original approach with the user pulling on a string on their glove to open it. What other game has that?\n-The art style is very simple and lightweight as seen in the videos/screenshots,\n-It is a relaxing experience. I fell asleep in my chair chilling with my Waba.\n-The developer is SUPER nice and receptive to feedback and has a very large vision for- and commitment to- Waba. Waba has been in development for over three years, and Edwon wanted to make sure he had it polished before he put it up on Steam. Go join the Discord and chat with him!\n-Waba is only $5. A Big Mac will not make you smile as much, and Waba does not come with the guilt and regret after eating one. \n\nCons:\n\n- At the time of this review (day of release) Waba makes a lot of repetitive noises. Edwon is working on it already.\n- There is not a lot of content in the game at this point, and this will change over time. Do not forget this is an early access game made by one person. The creation of animations, code, and models takes time. It is coming.\n\nI would recommend buying this game. Watch it grow. Be part of it. While you wait for additions, play with your new best friend, Waba. People who do want pets but do not have time or a place for them should definitely buy this game. I found myself grinning behind my headset the whole time.\n\nAlso, I am editing this to let WMR users know that I bit the bullet not knowing if it would work, and the game works great on my Dell VIsor.",
